    "title": "Ag Revolution signs with Ellis Park, IHRA - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nHENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — An agriculture supply company with roots in the Tri-State signs several deals to expand its visibility.\nEvansville based Ag Revolution has signed deals with Ellis Park and with the International Hot Rod Association to become an official sponsor of both organizations. That means Ag Revolution will provide Fendt and Massey Ferguson brand track equipment at Ellis Park and at IHRA races and tractor pulls.\nAg Revolution has 61 facilities across the Midwest, including locations in Henderson, Evansville and Vincennes.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "HENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — An agriculture supply company with roots in the Tri-State signs several deals to expand its visibility. Evansville based Ag Revolution has signed deals with Ellis Park and with the International Hot Rod Association to become an official sponsor of both organizations. That means Ag Revolution will provide Fendt and Massey Ferguson brand track equipment at Ellis Park and at IHRA races and tractor pulls. Ag Revolution has 61 facilities across the Midwest, including locations in Henderson, Evansville and Vincennes. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
